  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      151.75,
      302.53,
      391.79,
      338.2
    ],
    "text": "4.The following new Article is hereby insertedimmediately after Article 154E of the Constitution and shallhave effect as Article 154EE of the Constitution:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman",
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      205.75,
      351.73,
      391.79,
      473.56
    ],
    "text": "154EE. In the event of dissolution of anyProvincial Council by reason of the operationof the provisions of sub-paragraph (c) ofparagraph (8) of Article 154B or by any otherreason specified in any law, the powers of suchProvincial Council shall be exercised by theParliament until the specified date and theprovisions of Articles 154L and 154M shall,mutatis mutandis apply in relation to the exerciseof powers of the Provincial Council.\u201d.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      151.75,
      487.09,
      391.79,
      510.4
    ],
    "text": "5.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman",
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
